# Privacy-only exclusions
#
# Market data, normalized data, derived data, research reports, and source code
# are intentionally NOT ignored. Keep analysis-critical material versioned.

# Environment files may contain credentials. Templates remain publishable.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.template

# Authentication credentials and private keys.
.netrc
credentials.json
secrets.json
auth.json
tokens.json
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
id_rsa
id_ed25519

# Local/private configuration. Publish redacted examples separately.
config/local.*
config/private.*
config/secrets.*
config/credentials.*

# Explicit privacy convention for personal inputs at any directory level.
# Examples: portfolio/private/, decision_journal/private/, data/private/.
private/
**/private/
*.private.*
